(Analyst, Brokerage One: Can you explain what is driving the order book, and how worried) Tj T*
(should we be about Chinese imports?) Tj T*
(Rahul Mehta: The order book stands at 3,900 crore rupees, up 18 percent from the last) Tj T*
(quarter, and enquiries from European customers have increased.) Tj T*
(Chinese imports remain a risk to pricing in two product lines and we are watching anti-) Tj T*
(dumping duty decisions closely.) Tj T*
(Analyst, Brokerage Two: What is your thinking on acquisitions and the share buyback?) Tj T*
(Anita Rao: We are not planning a share buyback this year, and we will consider small) Tj T*
(acquisitions only if they add to our specialty portfolio.) Tj T*
(Moderator: Thank you. That concludes the call.) Tj T*
ET
